[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
I could not reproduce the outage. End-to-end connectivity from host_1_1_1_1 to the entire data center is healthy right now. From host_1_1_1_1, ICMP to the data center subnet succeeds (pings to 10.200.0.2–.6 all 0% loss, sub‑3 ms RTT). HTTP connectivity is also good (curl to each web_server IP returns in ~2 ms total). The DNS server at 10.200.0.2 responds to ICMP, and the host’s network stack is correctly configured with 10.1.1.2/24 and default gateway 10.1.1.1. Topology-wide probes confirm bidirectional reachability between hosts and servers. 

Mechanism: Because both ICMP and TCP/HTTP traffic traverse successfully with low latency and no loss, the L2/L3 path across the access switch, distribution switch (switch_dist_1_1), core (router_core_1/3), and server access fabric is operating normally. 

Localization: No faults observed on host_1_1_1_1, the building uplink (switch_dist_1_1 ↔ router_core_1), or the server side (switch_server_access and web servers). 

Root cause: Not reproducible; the reported “data center vanished” condition appears to have been transient or client-layer (e.g., local app/DNS cache), not a persistent network infrastructure fault. 

Corrective fix: No changes applied. If the issue recurs, capture timing and names/IPs affected and check the client’s resolver (/etc/resolv.conf) and application before escalating; concurrently, collect interface/OSPF status on switch_dist_1_1 and router_core_1 to catch any fleeting flaps. For now, service is restored and stable. 
=== END ===